WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
BUILD 059. A LEGAL CITATION CAN LOOK CONVINCING AND STILL FAIL. An AI-generated citation may be nonexistent, misquoted, out of jurisdiction, outdated, negatively treated, or irrelevant to the proposition it appears to support.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
USE A FICTIONAL RECORD. IN RE NORTHSTAR · 999 F.9TH 101. The citation, court, reporter, quotation, proposition, dates, jurisdiction, and treatment in this film are synthetic teaching fixtures—not real legal authority.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
PASS EACH GATE. EXISTENCE · QUOTE · PROPOSITION. Check separately whether the authority exists, the quoted language appears at the exact locator, and the source actually supports the precise claim made.

4
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.000
CHECK THE LEGAL CONTEXT. JURISDICTION · STATUS · TREATMENT. Keep court, hierarchy, date, version, subsequent history, negative treatment, citator coverage, and unresolved conflicts visible rather than collapsing them into one badge.

5
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.000
BOUND THE RESULT. A GATE IS NOT GOOD LAW. The demo performs no legal research or advice and cannot establish real existence, currentness, precedential value, proposition support, treatment, completeness, reliability, or safe reliance.

6
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.000
SAVE THIS. VERIFY BEFORE YOU RELY. A LEGAL CITATION BECOMES REVIEWABLE ONLY WHEN EXISTENCE, EXACT LANGUAGE, PROPOSITION, JURISDICTION, STATUS, TREATMENT, AND COVERAGE STAY DISTINCT.

